  <description>Two 18650 Li-ion cells in series in a side-by-side holder (about 75 x 40 mm), top view. Cell 1 (top) has its plus end on the right, cell 2 (bottom) has its plus end on the left; the holder strap on the right joins cell 1 plus to cell 2 minus (the midpoint). PACK- (black) leaves the LEFT short edge at cell 1 minus, PACK+ (red) the LEFT edge at cell 2 plus, and BAL (white, the midpoint) the RIGHT edge at the strap. Works in the Fritzing 1.0 simulator: the spice model is two 3.7 V sources, each with its own series internal resistance, stacked PACK- -&gt; cell 1 -&gt; BAL -&gt; cell 2 -&gt; PACK+, so PACK+ to PACK- reads 7.4 V and BAL to PACK- reads 3.7 V. The spice block follows the core part 4 x AAA Battery Mount.fzp. The model reads the cell voltage and internal resistance (per cell) properties; voltage is the nominal pack voltage shown in the Inspector.

Sources:
https://fritzing.org/
https://github.com/fritzing/fritzing-parts/blob/develop/core/4%20x%20AAA%20Battery%20Mount.fzp

Generated by fritzkit (https://github.com/pmaxhogan/fritzkit). Part artwork and data (c) 2026 fritzkit, licensed CC-BY-SA 3.0 like the Fritzing parts library.</description>
  <spice>
    <line>V{instanceTitle}A {net connector2}_{instanceTitle}_aux1 {net connector0} DC {cell voltage}</line>
    <line>R{instanceTitle}A {net connector2}_{instanceTitle}_aux1 {net connector2} {internal resistance}</line>
    <line>V{instanceTitle}B {net connector1}_{instanceTitle}_aux2 {net connector2} DC {cell voltage}</line>
    <line>R{instanceTitle}B {net connector1}_{instanceTitle}_aux2 {net connector1} {internal resistance}</line>
  </spice>
